        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "decc745b-5c3a-5400-ac99-6eff30bad109",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harold Ramis, Bill Murray, Andie MacDowell, Chris Elliott, Jennifer Celotta, Marita Geraghty\n- Works: Caddyshack, National Lampoon's Vacation, Groundhog Day, Analyze This, A Benihana Christmas\n- Roles: actor, director, writer, comedian\n\nFacts:\n- Harold Ramis was born on November 21, 1944, and he was an American actor, director, writer, and comedian.\n- Harold Ramis directed the comedy film Caddyshack, which was released in 1980.\n- Harold Ramis directed the comedy film National Lampoon's Vacation, which was released in 1983.\n- Harold Ramis directed the 1993 American fantasy-comedy film Groundhog Day.\n- Groundhog Day starred Bill Murray, Andie MacDowell, and Chris Elliott.\n- Marita Geraghty played Nancy Taylor in Groundhog Day.\n- Harold Ramis directed the episode A Benihana Christmas, and Jennifer Celotta wrote it.\n- Harold Ramis directed the comedy film Analyze This, which was released in 1999.\n- Harold Ramis died on February 24, 2014.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
